^YTT(601.95,127,1,757,0)="er: <.Patient_Gender.>\r\n|  \r\n|   ASRS-Screening Scale score = <-Total->\r\n|  \r\n|   The total score range is between 0 and 25. A score of 14 or higher is \r\n|   considered clinically significant, indicating the need for additional \r"
^YTT(601.95,127,1,758,0)="\n|   assessment. This test is intended for use as a screening tool only and \r\n|   should not be used in isolation to diagnose ADD\/ADHD without additional \r\n|   supporting evidence such as collateral information, academic\/occupational"
^YTT(601.95,127,1,759,0)=" \r\n|   records, and a thorough psychosocial history. For the purposes of \r\n|   diagnosing ADD\/ADHD, cognitive testing has decreased reliability and \r\n|   validity and is not required for diagnosis and treatment.\r\n|  \r\n|\r\n|Quest"
^YTT(601.95,127,1,760,0)="ions and Answers:\r\n|  \r\n|   1.  How often do you have difficulty concentrating on what people say to \r\n|       you, even when they are speaking to you directly?\r\n|       <*Answer_8695*>\r\n|   2.  How often do you leave your seat in"
