^YTT(601.95,277,1,165,0)="   Brief Addiction Monitor: IOP version (BAM-IOP-CSG-SUD)\r\n|    \r\n|    Date Given: <.Date_Given.>\r\n|    Clinician: <.Staff_Ordered_By.>\r\n|    Location: <.Location.>\r\n|    \r\n|    Veteran: <.Patient_Name_Last_First.>\r\n|    SSN: "
^YTT(601.95,277,1,166,0)="<.Patient_SSN.>\r\n|    DOB: <.Patient_Date_Of_Birth.> (<.Patient_Age.>)\r\n|    Gender: <.Patient_Gender.>\r\n|    \r\n|    \r\n|    Clinical Subscales:\r\n|   \r\n|       Use: <-Use->\r\n|       Items 4, 5A, 6. A high score indicates more"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,167,0)=" use, range is 0 to 12. If\r\n|       a patient scores a 1 or greater, it calls for further assessment and \r\n|       clinical attention, e.g., consider addition\/change of pharmacotherapy\r\n|       or psychosocial intervention.\r\n|    \"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,168,0)="r\n|       Risk Factors: <-Risk Factors->\r\n|       Items 1, 2, 3, 8, 11, 15. A high score indicates increased risk, range\r\n|       is 0 to 24. Clinicians are encouraged to consider scores on individual\r\n|       Risk items in offering "
^YTT(601.95,277,1,169,0)="interventions as indicated during initial \r\n|       treatment planning and following re-assessment.\r\n|       \r\n|       Protective Factors: <-Protective Factors->\r\n|       Items 9, 10, 12, 13, 14, 16. A high score indicates greater p"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,170,0)="rotective\r\n|       factors, range is 0 to 24. Clinicians are encouraged to consider scores"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,171,0)="\r\n|       on individual Protective items in offering interventions as indicated \r\n|       during initial treatment planning and following re-assessment.\r\n|\r\n|       Average Drinks   (5B): <*Answer_9156*> \r\n|       Highest Consumed"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,172,0)=" (5C): <*Answer_9157*>\r\n|       Items 5B and 5C should be reviewed and interpreted at the item-level \r\n|       and are not included in any composite scores. These items provide \r\n|       additional, clinically useful information about"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,173,0)=" quantity of alcohol use\r\n|       that users are encouraged to review and monitor, in addition to the \r\n|       frequency of use, risk and protective composite scores, to inform \r\n|       treatment planning and treatment progress.\r\n"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,174,0)="|   \r\n|   Questions and Answers\r\n|    \r\n|     A. Date of administration:\r\n|        <*Answer_9131*>\r\n|     B. Method of administration:\r\n|        <*Answer_9132*>\r\n|    \r\n|     1. In the past 7 days, how would you say your phy"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,175,0)="sical health has been?\r\n|        <*Answer_9133*>\r\n|    \r\n|     2. In the past 7 days, how many nights did you have trouble falling\r\n|        asleep or staying asleep?\r\n|        <*Answer_9134*>\r\n|    \r\n|     3. In the past 7 da"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,176,0)="ys, how many days have you felt depressed, anxious,\r\n|        angry or very upset throughout most of the day?\r\n|        <*Answer_9135*>\r\n|    \r\n|     4. In the past 7 days, how many days did you drink ANY alcohol?\r\n|        <*Answ"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,177,0)="er_9136*>\r\n|    \r\n|    5A. In the past 7 days, how many days did you have at least 5 drinks (if \r\n|        you are a man) or at least 4 drinks (if you are a woman)?\r\n|        [One drink is considered one shot of hard liquor (1.5 oz."
^YTT(601.95,277,1,178,0)=") or 12-ounce\r\n|        can\/bottle of beer or 5 ounce glass of wine.]\r\n|        <*Answer_9137*>\r\n|\r\n|    5B. In the past 7 days, on the days that you consumed alcohol, what was\r\n|        the average number of drinks you consumed "
^YTT(601.95,277,1,179,0)="on those days?\r\n|        <*Answer_9156*>\r\n| \r\n|    5C. In the past 7 days, on the days that you consumed alcohol, what was \r\n|        the highest number of drinks you consumed in one day?\r\n|        <*Answer_9157*>\r\n|    \r\n|   "
^YTT(601.95,277,1,180,0)="  6. In the past 7 days, how many days did you use any illegal or street\r\n|        drugs or abuse any prescription medications?\r\n|        <*Answer_9138*>\r\n|    \r\n|     7. In the past 7 days, how many days did you use any of the foll"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,181,0)="owing \r\n|        drugs:\r\n|    \r\n|        7A. Marijuana (cannabis, pot, weed)?\r\n|            <*Answer_9139*>\r\n|        7B. Sedatives and\/or Tranquilizers (benzos, Valium, Xanax, Ativan,\r\n|            Ambien, barbs, Phenobarbital"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,182,0)=", downers, etc.)?\r\n|            <*Answer_9140*>\r\n|        7C. Cocaine and\/or Crack?\r\n|            <*Answer_9141*>\r\n|        7D. Other Stimulants (amphetamine, methamphetamine, Dexedrine,\r\n|            Ritalin, Adderall, speed, cr"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,183,0)="ystal meth, ice, etc.)?\r\n|            <*Answer_9142*>\r\n|        7E. Opiates (Heroin, Morphine, Dilaudid, Demerol, Oxycontin, oxy,\r\n|            codeine (Tylenol 2,3,4), Percocet, Vicodin, Fentanyl, etc.)?\r\n|            <*Answer_9143"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,184,0)="*>\r\n|        7F. Inhalants (glues, adhesives, nail polish remover, paint thinner, \r\n|            etc.)?\r\n|            <*Answer_9144*>\r\n|        7G. Other drugs (steroids, non-prescription sleep and diet pills, \r\n|            Benad"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,185,0)="ryl, Ephedra, other over-the-counter or unknown medications)?\r\n|            <*Answer_9145*>\r\n|    \r\n|     8. In the past 7 days, how much were you bothered by cravings or urges\r\n|        to drink alcohol or use drugs?\r\n|        <*"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,186,0)="Answer_9146*>\r\n|    \r\n|     9. How confident are you that you will NOT use alcohol and drugs in the\r\n|        next 7 days?\r\n|        <*Answer_9147*>\r\n|    \r\n|    10. In the past 7 days, how many days did you attend self-help mee"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,187,0)="tings\r\n|        like AA or NA to support your recovery?\r\n|        <*Answer_9148*>\r\n|    "
^YTT(601.95,277,1,188,0)="\r\n|    11. In the past 7 days, how many days were you in any situations or with \r\n|        any people that might put you at an increased risk for using alcohol\r\n|        or drugs (i.e., around risky \""people, places or things\"")?\r\n|"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,189,0)="        <*Answer_9149*>\r\n|    \r\n|    12. Does your religion or spirituality help support your recovery?\r\n|        <*Answer_9150*>\r\n|    \r\n|    13. In the past 7 days, how many days did you spend much of the time at\r\n|        wor"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,190,0)="k, school, or doing volunteer work?\r\n|        <*Answer_9151*>\r\n|    \r\n|    14. Do you have enough income (from legal sources) to pay for necessities\r\n|        such as housing, transportation, food and clothing for yourself and\r\n| "
^YTT(601.95,277,1,191,0)="       your dependents?\r\n|        <*Answer_9152*>\r\n|    \r\n|    15. In the past 7 days, how much have you been bothered by arguments or \r\n|        problems getting along with any family members or friends?\r\n|        <*Answer_9153*>"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,192,0)="\r\n|    \r\n|    16. In the past 7 days, how many days did you contact or spend time with\r\n|        any family members or friends who are supportive of your recovery?\r\n|        <*Answer_9154*>\r\n|    \r\n|    17. How satisfied are you"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,193,0)=" with your progress toward achieving your\r\n|        recovery goals?\r\n|        <*Answer_9155*>\r\n|    \r\n|     Information contained in this note is based on a self-report assessment and is not sufficient to use alone for diagnostic pu"
^YTT(601.95,277,1,194,0)="rposes.  \r\nAssessment results should be verified for accuracy and used in conjunction with other diagnostic activities and procedures.""},""rule"":[{""booleanOperator"":""AND"",""consistencyCheck"":null,""id"":408,""indexOperator"":""Equals"",""indexQues"
