^YTT(601.95,435,1,116,0)="inician: <.Staff_Ordered_By.>\r\n|   Location:  <.Location.>\r\n|  \r\n|   Veteran:  <.Patient_Name_Last_First.>\r\n|   SSN: <.Patient_SSN.>\r\n|   DOB: <.Patient_Date_Of_Birth.> (<.Patient_Age.>)\r\n|   Gender: <.Patient_Gender.>\r\n|  \r\"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,117,0)="n|   PCL-5 DAILY Total Score = <-PCL-5 DAILY->\r\n|\r\n|   This measure assesses an individual's perception of the distress \r\n|   associated with possible PTSD symptoms. It is not used to diagnose \r\n|   PTSD. Symptoms are rated from 0-4"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,118,0)=" in terms of distress they cause \r\n|   the individual.  Scores that are greater than or equal to 31-33 \r\n|   suggest that the veteran may meet the criteria for a PTSD diagnosis.\r\n|   However, it is important to use caution when using "
^YTT(601.95,435,1,119,0)="this cutoff since \r\n|   it is possible for some Veterans with scores lower than 31-33 to meet "
^YTT(601.95,435,1,120,0)="\r\n|   criteria for PTSD.  Additional testing using a structured diagnostic \r\n|   interview, such as the Clinician Administered PTSD Scale for DSM-5, \r\n|   is recommended to confirm diagnostic status.\r\n|\r\n|   Values range from 0 to"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,121,0)=" 80 with higher scores indicating more probable \r\n|   PTSD.\r\n|  \r\n|Questions and Answers:\r\n|  \r\n|   1.  Repeated, disturbing, and unwanted memories of the stressful \r\n|       experience?\r\n|       <*Answer_9230*>\r\n|   2.  Rep"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,122,0)="eated, disturbing dreams of the stressful experience?\r\n|       <*Answer_9231*>\r\n|   3.  Suddenly feeling or acting as if the stressful experience were \r\n|       actually happening again (as if you were actually back there \r\n|       "
^YTT(601.95,435,1,123,0)="reliving it)?\r\n|       <*Answer_9232*>\r\n|   4.  Feeling very upset when something reminded you of the stressful\r\n|       experience?\r\n|       <*Answer_9233*>\r\n|   5.  Having strong physical reactions when something reminded you of"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,124,0)=" the\r\n|       stressful experience (for example, heart pounding, trouble breathing,\r\n|       sweating)?\r\n|       <*Answer_9234*>\r\n|   6.  Avoiding memories, thoughts, or feelings related to the stressful\r\n|       experience?\r\n| "
^YTT(601.95,435,1,125,0)="      <*Answer_9235*>\r\n|   7.  Avoiding external reminders of the stressful experience (for example,\r\n|       people, places, conversations, activities, objects, or situations)?\r\n|       <*Answer_9236*>\r\n|   8.  Trouble remembering "
^YTT(601.95,435,1,126,0)="important parts of the stressful experience?\r\n|       <*Answer_9237*>\r\n|   9.  Having strong negative beliefs about yourself, other people, or the\r\n|       world (for example, having thoughts such as: I am bad, there is\r\n|       som"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,127,0)="ething seriously wrong with me, no one can be trusted, the world\r\n|       is completely dangerous)?\r\n|       <*Answer_9238*>\r\n|  10.  Blaming yourself or someone else for the stressful experience or what\r\n|       happened after it?\"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,128,0)="r\n|       <*Answer_9239*>\r\n|  11.  Having strong negative feelings such as fear, horror, anger, guilt, or\r\n|       shame?\r\n|       <*Answer_9240*>\r\n|  12.  Loss of interest in activities that you used to enjoy?\r\n|       <*Answer_"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,129,0)="9241*>\r\n|  13.  Feeling distant or cut off from other people?\r\n|       <*Answer_9242*>\r\n|  14.  Trouble experiencing positive feelings (for example, being unable to \r\n|       feel happiness or have loving feelings for people close t"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,130,0)="o you)?\r\n|       <*Answer_9243*>\r\n|  15.  Irritable behavior, angry outbursts, or acting aggressively?\r\n|       <*Answer_9244*>\r\n|  16.  Taking too many risks or doing things that could cause you harm?\r\n|       <*Answer_9245*>\r\n"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,131,0)="|  17.  Being \""super alert\"" or watchful or on guard?\r\n|       <*Answer_9246*>\r\n|  18.  Feeling jumpy or easily startled?\r\n|       <*Answer_9247*>\r\n|  19.  Having difficulty concentrating?\r\n|       <*Answer_9248*>\r\n|  20.  Trou"
^YTT(601.95,435,1,132,0)="ble falling or staying asleep?\r\n|       <*Answer_9249*>\r\n|  \r\n|Information contained in this note is based on a self-report assessment \r\n|and is not sufficient to use alone for diagnostic purposes. Assessment \r\n|results should be "
^YTT(601.95,435,1,133,0)="verified for accuracy and used in conjunction with \r\n|other diagnostic activities.""},""scaleGroup"":[{""grid1"":0,""grid2"":0,""grid3"":0,""id"":395,""instrument"":326,""name"":""PCL-5 DAILY"",""ordInc"":10,""ordMax"":80,""ordMin"":0,""ordTitle"":""Score"",""scale"""
