^YTT(601.95,553,1,10,0)="troText"":""Terms used in next item. CONSTANTLY MOIST: Skin is kept moist almost constantly by perspiration, urine, etc. Dampness is detected every time patient is moved or turned. VERY MOIST: Skin is often, but \r\n not always, moist. Linen "
^YTT(601.95,553,1,11,0)="must be changed at least once a shift. OCCASIONALLY MOIST: Skin is occasionally moist, requiring an extra linen change about once a day. RARELY MOIST: Skin is usually dry;  \r\nlinen requires changing at routine intervals."",""max"":0,""min"":0,"
